r of users  can test it as a canary deployment and  start giving you feedback so we're  trying to build that into our cloud  we've seen the rise of DevOps practices  up out in the industry but now we're  building into our products with products  like cloud code like managed kubernetes  and CSP  cloud run our new server lists offering  just really reducing the barriers to  anyone like a Google engineer can build  code and get it in production as easily  as possible  fantastic now if you had to pick just  one just one best practice from  yesterday's keynote that you want  developers to walk away with what would  it be I'm gonna cheat a little and  instead of like I think Google said I  really like what twinkle desai said who  is a VP at Kohl's who started her career  as a developer and a UNIX is admin and  she built a lot of automation at calls  now she runs couple years later she runs  a 200-person team they have a hundred  micro services five thousand containers  it's all automated it's running on  manage gke on Prem she said they've been  through two big holiday shopping windows  which you know in retail is a really big  deal so I'm thrilled that Google cloud  can support retail customers but by  making her people super productive it's  been really great for calls and really  great for her career that's an  inspirational customer story we also saw  incredible demos during the keynote  yesterday can you tell us about some of  them and which one was your favorite ah  there was a couple that were a lot of  fun I really like what Wix is doing with  Google cloud you know they've gone from  being like a drag and drop web  environment but now it's totally totally  programmable and extensible at Google  Cloud that's really exciting the opening  demo that that Mandy Waite led us  through like her dev team is taking us  through was very very cool because it  was a mix of developers doing VM based  development with Jenkins for deployment  of new VM images a container based app  in the middle and then extending with  new services with functions serverless  functions which is pretty cool so to see  all those teams kind of working together  and using tools like cloud code our new  IDE integration for vs code and IntelliJ  just awesome people can work the way  they want to work it all works together  all runs at Google cloud seamlessly one  pane of glass with stack driver to  observe and manage it and I think that's  great let developers do what they want  and get to the fun parts that's  fantastic thank you so much again for  joining us today and giving us some of  that great information  [Music]

